# Project: GridGuard AI — Intelligent Electricity Loss Localization

Act as a senior full-stack developer, data engineer, and UI/UX designer. Build a complete, working hackathon prototype called **GridGuard AI**, a smart electricity distribution monitoring and loss-localization platform.

Do not merely create a static UI or a landing page. Build an interactive application with working simulations, calculations, charts, network visualization, anomaly detection, and investigation workflows.

## 1. Problem Statement

A rural electricity feeder supplies 60 houses. The transformer meter records 18% more energy than all 60 household meters record collectively. The discrepancy increases between 7 PM and 10 PM and falls again by midnight. Physical inspections have not identified the cause.

The hints are:

1. The missing energy is being consumed or lost somewhere between two meters.
2. Measuring the same electrical quantity at carefully selected points helps narrow down where the discrepancy occurs. Measurement placement matters more than measurement frequency alone.

The objective is to detect unexplained energy discrepancies, identify suspicious distribution sections, and narrow down a simulated unauthorized connection using strategically placed measurement points.

Important: An energy discrepancy does not automatically prove theft. Account for technical losses, measurement errors, missing readings, and legitimate loads. Exact connection localization must rely on sufficiently detailed measurements. Never falsely accuse a real household.

